      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely natural to feel that jitters before a major event; that feeling is just your high standards kicking in! A truly professional timeline doesn't just list tasks; it anticipates failures. I've integrated specific \"Go/No-Go\" contingency checks throughout the schedule to catch those small, insidious problems before they escalate into full-blown logistical nightmares.\n\n***\n\n**Day 1 Opening Ceremony: Logistical Timeline with Contingency Buffers (06:00 – 09:30)**\n\n| Time Slot | Duration | Activity | Responsible Team | Contingency Check / Buffer |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **06:00 – 07:00** | 60 min | Venue Access & Core Setup | Logistics/Venue Team | **Check 1 (Power Grid):** Confirm all primary and backup power sources are stable. *If any flicker, halt setup and log issue immediately.* |\n| **07:00 – 07:45** | 45 min | Catering Arrival & Breakfast Setup | Catering Team | **Check 2 (Service Readiness):** Walk-through with Catering",
